# What the site build does not need.
#
# The deploy runs from the repo root, because site/ui is a workspace package and
# its dependencies are built from source. That would otherwise upload the whole
# company: strategy, the planning documents had no part in
# building a component gallery, so they did not leave the machine.
#
# Leading slash matters: `docs/` is a gitignore-style pattern and would also
# match `cortex/docs` and `helix/docs`, which are workspace members. Excluding
# those breaks `bun install` before the build starts.
#
# **Amended 25 Aug 2026, and the old rule had started doing the harm it warns
# about one line up.** `/docs/` was written when that folder held the numbered
# strategy and nothing else. Two things have changed since: the strategy left
# with the history rewrite, so the exclusion now protects nothing that exists,
# and `site/content` became `docs/insights`, so the folder holds
# `@fusion-io/insights`, a workspace member the site depends on. Excluding it
# failed `bun install` exactly as this comment predicted for the nested ones.
#
# So the pattern names the files rather than the folder. The three markdown
# documents left at the top of `docs/` are the queue and two generated
# references, none of them read by anything on the build path and all three
# repository-internal, which `site/ui/app/helix/tokens.json/route.ts` says of
# the token reference in as many words.
/docs/*.md

# Build output and scratch, rebuilt on Vercel anyway.
.claude/
.local/
target/
**/.next/
**/.turbo/
**/dist/
**/node_modules/

# Rust, which nothing in this project builds.
Cargo.lock
Cargo.toml
